DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T120000
SUMMARY:Data Days Hotline: No Slides\, Just Answers
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nThis is not a polished talk. This i
 s a hotline.\n\nThe questions come straight from the community. You send t
 hem in\, we play them live\, and our experts jump in to figure it out in r
 eal time. No scripts\, no slides\, no perfect answers\, just honest help\,
  ideas\, and the occasional “let’s try this.”\n\nWhether you’re st
 uck\, curious\, or just want to hear how others are solving things in Micr
 osoft Fabric\, SQL\, Power BI\, and AI\, this is where it all comes togeth
 er. You’ll learn something\, hear different perspectives\, and probably 
 realize you’re not the only one asking that question.\n\nPre-requisites:
 \nFind ways to connect: https://aka.ms/dd/connect\nSee what else is happen
 ing during Data Days: https://aka.ms/datadays
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3153
 33862/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260619T210410Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260619T210410Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_315274179@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260623T042124Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T140000
SUMMARY:Microsoft IQ Deep Dive with Python: Foundry IQ
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn the first session of our Microso
 ft IQ Deep Dive with Python series\, we’ll kick things off with an intro
 duction to the Microsoft IQ family: Foundry IQ\, Work IQ\, Fabric IQ\, and
  Web IQ.\n\nWe’ll then take a deeper look at Foundry IQ (Azure AI Search
 )\, exploring how it helps agents and applications work with curated knowl
 edge and organizational context.\n\nWe'll build a knowledge base and conne
 ct it to multiple knowledge sources\, including the new IQs\, MCP servers\
 , and search indexes built from ingested data.\n\nThen we'll perform multi
 -source agentic retrieval on the knowledge base\, which executes queries i
 n parallel and merges the results with state-of-the-art ranking models.\n\
 nFinally\, we will build an agent in Python using Microsoft Agent Framewor
 k and ground the agent's responses in results from the Foundry IQ knowledg
 e base.\n\nAll code demos will use Python and will be available in an open
 -source repository for you to deploy yourself. After the stream\, join off
 ice hours in the [Microsoft Foundry Discord](http://aka.ms/aipython/oh) to
  ask follow-up questions.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3152
 74179/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260615T182632Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260615T182632Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_315274189@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260623T042124Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T140000
SUMMARY:Microsoft IQ Deep Dive with Python: Work IQ
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn the second session of our Micros
 oft IQ Deep Dive with Python series\, we’ll focus on Work IQ and how it 
 brings workplace context into AI-powered experiences.\n\nWe’ll explore h
 ow developers can use Work IQ through APIs\, A2A patterns\, MCP integratio
 n\, and tool-based workflows.\n\nWe’ll look at two practical tool exampl
 es\, then show how Work IQ can be used from Copilot and from a Microsoft A
 gent Framework agent. All code demos will use Python and will be available
  in an open-source repository for you to deploy yourself.\n\nAfter the str
 eam\, join office hours in the [Microsoft Foundry Discord](http://aka.ms/a
 ipython/oh) to ask follow-up questions.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3152
 74189/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260615T182711Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260615T182711Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_315334476@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260623T042124Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T120000
SUMMARY:Data Days Lightning Talks: Short Talks. Big Ideas. Zero Fluff.
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nWhat happens when you give really s
 mart people 5 minutes and say “go”?\n\nWe’re bringing together MVPs\
 , community builders\, and experts for a rapid-fire series of 5-minute tal
 ks on things they’re excited about right now. No long intros. No overthi
 nking. Just idea after idea after idea. Zero time to get bored.\n\nYou’l
 l hear fresh takes\, clever tips\, and things you didn’t know you needed
  to learn across Microsoft Fabric\, SQL\, Power BI\, and AI. It’s fast\,
  it’s fun\, and by the end you’ll have more ideas than you know what t
 o do with.\n\nPre-requisites:\nFind ways to connect: https://aka.ms/dd/con
 nect\nSee what else is happening during Data Days: https://aka.ms/datadays
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3153
 34476/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260619T220637Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260619T220637Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_315274210@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260623T042124Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T140000
SUMMARY:Microsoft IQ Deep Dive with Python: Fabric IQ
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn the final session of our Microso
 ft IQ Deep Dive with Python series\, we’ll explore Fabric IQ and how it 
 connects AI experiences to structured business data.\n\nWe’ll introduce 
 the key concepts behind Fabric IQ\, including ontologies and data agents\,
  and show how they help describe\, organize\, and reason over operational 
 data stored in OneLake.\n\nWe’ll use the Microsoft Fabric API SDK in Pyt
 hon to connect to Fabric IQ\, so that we can programmatically configure on
 tologies and answer questions about our data.\n\nAll code demos will use P
 ython and will be available in an open-source repository for you to deploy
  yourself.\n\nAfter the stream\, join office hours in the [Microsoft Found
 ry Discord](http://aka.ms/aipython/oh) to ask follow-up questions.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3152
 74210/
